{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass after these things.</b> Rashi: on Mount Moriah, on his way back, Abraham was reflecting and said: had it been my son, etc. And if you ask: but in the pericope of Lekh Lekha, regarding אחר הדברים האלה, Rashi explained that wherever 'אחר' is said it is close by, but where 'אחרי' is said it is distant — and where do we find 'אחרי' meaning close by? One may answer: 'אחר' is exclusively close by, while 'אחרי' is sometimes distant and sometimes close by. This fits the order of the pericope of Vayera."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:20.646182269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}